WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:04.220
Hold onto your heads and watch your step
around the giant pit of dead bodies,

00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:07.900
because we have the scariest horror
film if you happen to have hay fever.

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:12.680
Netflix's "In the Tall Grass" is a mind-bending
horror film from Vincenzo Natali

00:00:12.860 --> 00:00:15.780
based off the novella by
Stephen King and Joe Hill.

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:20.920
And in this video, we're going to be taking a deep dive into its ending and shed some light on the meaning of

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:26.020
the Black Rock, the church, the field,
the monsters, and the time loop itself.

00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:29.760
So follow me into the
grass, because here we go.

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:35.880
The ending of "In the Tall Grass" is actually the beginning, but this time the time loop has been broken.

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:39.560
Whereas the beginning of the film
sees Becky and Cal head into the grass,

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:41.760
the end sees them move away from it.

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:45.800
And that's all because of Tobin, who
we'll find is the key to breaking the loop.

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:51.120
But to fully understand the ending,
we must first understand the beginning.

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:54.480
Since the film, like
the field, is its own loop.

00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:57.160
We start outside the
church and we end there too.

00:00:57.360 --> 00:01:00.820
This time, however, with the characters
having grown through their journey.

00:01:00.980 --> 00:01:03.220
The first time Becky and
Cal head into the grass,

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:06.280
we're picking up clues as
to how the field operates.

00:01:06.460 --> 00:01:11.340
Everything about it is distorted:
direction, sound, and even time itself.

00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:13.979
When we later meet
Travis, Becky's ex-boyfriend,

00:01:13.980 --> 00:01:17.080
he tells Becky and Cal that
they've been gone for two months,

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:19.620
but for them, it's only been about a day.

00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:22.400
If one day in the field is two
months in the real world,

00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:29.140
we can speculate this loop has repeated at least 60 times since Becky and Cal's initial venture into the grass.

00:01:29.220 --> 00:01:32.660
This is how Travis is able to
see Becky's decomposed body.

00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:36.900
He is seeing a previous loop version of
her that wasn't successful at getting out.

00:01:36.940 --> 00:01:39.520
But before we get too into
the mysteries of the field,

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:44.040
it's important to know why Becky and Cal
are driving through Kansas in the first place.

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:49.540
Although you may think Becky's child is a subplot of
the film, it's actually what propels the story forward.

00:01:49.660 --> 00:01:54.240
You see, Becky used to be with Travis and
then she got pregnant, which Travis didn't like.

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:59.440
He left her and she decided to give the
child up for adoption to a family in San Diego.

00:01:59.620 --> 00:02:02.260
Hence, Becky and Cal
driving across the country.

00:02:02.360 --> 00:02:06.640
It's only at the end that Becky decides
to keep the baby and drive back home.

00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:09.460
The tall grass has given her redemption.

00:02:09.620 --> 00:02:12.880
Travis arguably has an
even stronger character arc.

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:15.940
He put himself and his career
before Becky and the child,

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:18.660
even encouraging
Becky via the "A Word".

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:21.140
I can't say it or YouTube
will demonetize me.

00:02:21.420 --> 00:02:27.240
Travis was a musician, just like Ross, but unlike
Ross didn't give up his career to focus on a family.

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:28.420
As Ross says,

00:02:35.480 --> 00:02:39.340
But as Travis goes on his own
journey, he sees the error of his ways,

00:02:39.460 --> 00:02:43.980
sacrificing himself so that the girl
he loves and his unborn child can live.

00:02:44.120 --> 00:02:49.940
He went from wanting to - rhymes with "cohort" -
his own child to sacrificing himself to save it.

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:51.720
Talk about a pretty big arc.

00:02:51.720 --> 00:02:55.420
But this whole ending would never
have taken place if it weren't for Tobin.

00:02:57.480 --> 00:03:01.520
He is the only character that is successfully
able to break free from the tall grass

00:03:01.520 --> 00:03:03.900
in order to stop the loop from continuing.

00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:08.200
About halfway through the movie, we
see Tobin beckoned into the grass by Travis.

00:03:08.380 --> 00:03:11.840
But Travis went into the grass
because he saw Becky's car,

00:03:12.060 --> 00:03:14.700
and Becky was beckoned
into the grass by Tobin.

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:19.540
This is the loop. It's kind of like asking
what came first, the chicken or the egg.

00:03:19.580 --> 00:03:23.540
There's no logical explanation
for who entered the field first.

00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:26.980
It's stuck in this loop,
bound to forever repeat itself.

00:03:26.980 --> 00:03:31.160
The film, however, does give us
some interesting clues in Easter eggs.

00:03:31.320 --> 00:03:36.860
For example, the novel Becky drops before she
heads into the field, the same one Travis picks up,

00:03:36.860 --> 00:03:40.400
is "Jane Eyre", the story of a
young woman coming into adulthood

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:43.900
who has a child with a man she
had a tumultuous relationship with.

00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:45.100
Sound familiar?

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:47.480
But to understand Travis's sacrifice,

00:03:47.540 --> 00:03:52.640
we must first take a look at the Humboldt family
and Ross's fascination with the Black Rock.

00:03:52.680 --> 00:03:56.100
The Black Rock, according to
Ross, predates Native Americans.

00:03:56.280 --> 00:04:02.820
It's the geographic center of North America and was carved even before the glaciers carried the hills away.

00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:05.820
Ross even calls it the
center of the center.

00:04:05.940 --> 00:04:07.980
On its surface are carved symbols,

00:04:07.980 --> 00:04:10.880
like this one with outstretched
hands, which we'll see later,

00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:13.660
and of the grass people
hoisting a pregnant woman.

00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:17.040
The carvings therefore are
a prophecy of what's to come.

00:04:17.160 --> 00:04:21.500
The Black Rock also happens to be the
name of the church outside the tall grass.

00:04:21.520 --> 00:04:24.000
In fact, it's called the Black
Rock of the Redeemer,

00:04:24.180 --> 00:04:28.940
because every character, with perhaps the
exception of Tobin, who does eventually get out,

00:04:29.020 --> 00:04:31.200
has something to
redeem about themselves.

00:04:31.380 --> 00:04:33.760
But this church isn't here to worship God.

00:04:33.860 --> 00:04:35.840
It's here to worship the Black Rock.

00:04:35.980 --> 00:04:41.100
There are no Christian symbols in it, no
pulpits, just a solitary locked door at the back.

00:04:41.320 --> 00:04:45.920
The closest thing you do get to a Christian
symbol are these carvings of a stained-glass here,

00:04:46.100 --> 00:04:48.700
but even the tint of it
is green, like the grass,

00:04:49.020 --> 00:04:51.160
green also symbolizing sickness.

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:55.640
At the back is a solitary door, which
can only be opened from the inside.

00:04:55.680 --> 00:04:59.400
Tobin is able to open it after
he's transported there by Travis.

00:04:59.500 --> 00:05:02.740
After Travis touched the Black
Rock, he was given its powers,

00:05:02.840 --> 00:05:05.940
powers which according to
the rock can help find a way out.

00:05:06.020 --> 00:05:10.540
By touching the Black Rock, Travis was
able to see the different holes within the field.

00:05:10.720 --> 00:05:15.540
We get a glimpse of such a hole when Freddy the
golden retriever moves through this hole here

00:05:15.540 --> 00:05:17.580
and winds up across from the church.

00:05:17.740 --> 00:05:21.260
It's these holes that Ross
also used to catch his victims.

00:05:21.260 --> 00:05:24.720
He could always catch them because
he knew where to go while they didn't,

00:05:24.880 --> 00:05:27.540
but the Black Rock
corrupts as it did to Ross,

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:30.260
slowly taking control of its victims.

00:05:30.340 --> 00:05:34.600
Ross used to be a Christian man so
much so that he was in a gospel band,

00:05:34.720 --> 00:05:39.660
but the Black Rock corrupted him, turning
his faith away from God and toward the Rock.

00:05:39.660 --> 00:05:43.840
When Becky has her child next to the
Black Rock, the ground beneath it splits open,

00:05:43.840 --> 00:05:47.220
revealing hundreds of souls
the Black Rock has corrupted.

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:50.540
Their hands reach upward,
almost as if pleading for help.

00:05:50.620 --> 00:05:52.960
We know countless others
have been brought into the field

00:05:52.960 --> 00:05:57.880
just by looking at the different eras of cars
that have collected dust in the church's parking lot,

00:05:58.080 --> 00:06:03.500
cars from the 50s, 60s, present day, and all from different states, according to the license plates.

00:06:03.620 --> 00:06:08.100
When Ross attacks Cal, we also see
more decomposed bodies laying in the field.

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:11.060
Who knows how many
litter its vast expanse?

00:06:11.180 --> 00:06:13.740
Then there's also the
question of the green people.

00:06:13.740 --> 00:06:15.880
That's what they're
called in the end credits.

00:06:16.040 --> 00:06:19.560
They are the force behind the Black Rock
and the people depicted on the carvings.

00:06:19.720 --> 00:06:21.840
They are different than the
people beneath the rock,

00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:25.480
their faces are made of grass and
they themselves are corrupted.

00:06:25.600 --> 00:06:27.280
When Ross's eyes turned green here,

00:06:27.320 --> 00:06:31.940
it's an indicator that the green people are
acting through Ross via the Black Rock.

00:06:32.060 --> 00:06:36.660
They can control the grass, bending it to
its will as well as move organic material,

00:06:36.880 --> 00:06:40.720
but once something is no longer living,
they lose the ability to control it.

00:06:40.780 --> 00:06:43.480
As Tobin says multiple
times throughout the film,

00:06:48.640 --> 00:06:54.060
The green people want flesh to fuel the grass
and lure more living things into its grasp.

00:06:54.100 --> 00:06:57.420
The decomposition of dead
bodies helps fertilize the land,

00:06:57.460 --> 00:07:00.300
and if the green people are
to survive, they need to feed.

00:07:00.540 --> 00:07:02.380
As Ross says later on in the film,

00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:13.880
Touching the Black Rock gives the possessed person a window into the field's many holes and branching paths,

00:07:14.140 --> 00:07:17.120
because it will help that
person track down more victims.

00:07:17.180 --> 00:07:18.720
It will help them see.

00:07:18.860 --> 00:07:21.760
Even when Ross loses all
of his eyesight, he says,

00:07:25.360 --> 00:07:29.420
Director Vincenzo Natali focuses
a lot on eyes throughout the film.

00:07:29.500 --> 00:07:31.360
Here's one of the opening shots of Becky,

00:07:31.540 --> 00:07:32.840
another of a dead crow,

00:07:33.020 --> 00:07:35.940
and check out this shot when
Travis touches the Black Rock.

00:07:36.120 --> 00:07:38.620
It looks just like the veins
coming out of an eye.

00:07:38.740 --> 00:07:44.120
Eyes being deceiving is also manifested in the
scene where Cal makes Becky eat her own child.

00:07:44.340 --> 00:07:46.820
Notice how the edges
of the screen are blurred,

00:07:46.940 --> 00:07:49.440
and how Cal magically turns into Ross.

00:07:49.900 --> 00:07:53.980
It calls into question whether what Becky
is seeing happened the way we think it did,

00:07:54.120 --> 00:07:58.740
or perhaps this did happen and what we're
seeing is just another unsuccessful loop.

00:07:58.980 --> 00:08:00.080
As Tobin says,

00:08:08.640 --> 00:08:11.840
In the final showdown, Ross tries to
make his son touch the Black Rock,

00:08:12.020 --> 00:08:14.460
once again bringing up
the theme of redemption.

00:08:18.980 --> 00:08:21.640
But didn't we already see
Tobin touch the Rock?

00:08:21.860 --> 00:08:23.980
How is he already not corrupted?

00:08:24.140 --> 00:08:29.360
We did, but this is a new loop, another
chance for our characters to redeem themselves.

00:08:29.460 --> 00:08:34.560
In the nick of time, Becky saves Tobin by
stabbing Ross with a Benny's Crab Shack necklace.

00:08:34.640 --> 00:08:38.180
We're never given too much
information as to the significance of this,

00:08:38.340 --> 00:08:43.320
but it's first seen when Travis enters the grass
and takes it from Becky's decomposing corpse.

00:08:43.440 --> 00:08:46.420
It seems that this item has
some sort of significance to him,

00:08:46.420 --> 00:08:50.480
perhaps it was a memento of a time he and
Becky spent together living in New Hampshire.

00:08:50.700 --> 00:08:53.740
I'm assuming that's where they're from
judging by Becky's New Hampshire plates,

00:08:53.800 --> 00:08:55.480
although it's never mentioned in the film.

00:08:55.620 --> 00:08:58.040
After Travis kills Ross and
touches the Black Rock,

00:08:58.220 --> 00:09:01.240
he's infused with the power
of being able to see the exit,

00:09:01.400 --> 00:09:04.920
and quickly takes off with Tobin
before the corruption can take over.

00:09:04.980 --> 00:09:07.780
He gives him the necklace
as proof that he loves crabs,

00:09:07.840 --> 00:09:09.840
I mean, he's telling the
truth about the grass.

00:09:09.980 --> 00:09:13.800
Becky and Cal decide not to go in the
grass, but Becky goes one step further,

00:09:13.940 --> 00:09:18.420
deciding to go the opposite way and drop
off Tobin at the police station in Topeka

00:09:18.600 --> 00:09:20.300
as well as keeping her baby.

00:09:20.420 --> 00:09:24.480
The events that unfolded in the grass
have somehow made her change her mind.

00:09:27.880 --> 00:09:32.160
With Tobin, Becky, and Cal no longer
going into the field, the loop has been closed,

00:09:32.300 --> 00:09:35.600
but this doesn't mean more
people can be swayed into its orbit.

00:09:35.660 --> 00:09:37.820
We did see all those
cars outside the church,

00:09:37.820 --> 00:09:40.340
so new loops will continually spring up,

00:09:40.540 --> 00:09:44.360
bringing its victims in an endless
cycle on the path to redemption.

00:09:44.580 --> 00:09:50.520
And a church, or at least a building that resembles
one, is such a fitting physical representation of this.

00:09:50.700 --> 00:09:54.260
The Christian faith is all about
finding redemption through Christ,

00:09:54.380 --> 00:09:56.900
absolving our sins
through the power of God.

00:09:57.040 --> 00:10:01.320
The Black Rock takes on this role,
offering redemption in a different form.

00:10:01.560 --> 00:10:04.920
One of the big flaws of this
film is Cal's redemptive arc.

00:10:04.920 --> 00:10:08.780
I felt like he didn't have one,
which makes it doubly unsatisfying,

00:10:08.820 --> 00:10:11.100
since his character
also gets out of the loop.

00:10:11.400 --> 00:10:13.520
His character really hasn't changed.

00:10:13.580 --> 00:10:17.400
The film sets up Cal's flaw as being
unable to let go of his sister,

00:10:17.580 --> 00:10:19.260
especially when it comes to Travis.

00:10:19.460 --> 00:10:21.020
This causes friction between the two,

00:10:21.100 --> 00:10:24.300
eventually culminating in him
throwing Travis from the Bowl-a-Rama.

00:10:24.400 --> 00:10:26.080
For Cal to have a satisfying arc,

00:10:26.080 --> 00:10:30.340
we'd need to see him accept letting
his sister go, but we never saw that.

00:10:30.480 --> 00:10:34.500
Instead, we see him pleading for her not
to go, which ends up getting him killed.

00:10:34.600 --> 00:10:36.600
His flaw leads to his own death,

00:10:36.840 --> 00:10:39.560
but he is still rewarded at the
end by getting out of the loop,

00:10:39.680 --> 00:10:42.640
something I would have changed
in the second act for his character

00:10:42.640 --> 00:10:45.220
in order to make the ending
more emotionally fulfilling.

00:10:45.440 --> 00:10:47.760
Overall, I enjoyed "In the Tall Grass",

00:10:47.780 --> 00:10:51.580
a lot more than some of the derivative horrors
that have been lately coming out in theaters.

00:10:51.800 --> 00:10:55.000
It's a film that makes you think,
has some gorgeous cinematography,

00:10:55.240 --> 00:10:57.340
and didn't feature any
children of the corn.

00:10:57.580 --> 00:10:58.920
I hope you enjoyed this video.

00:10:59.000 --> 00:11:01.340
Let me know what you thought of
the movie in the comments below,

00:11:01.580 --> 00:11:06.140
and please give it a thumbs up and subscribe
with the bell on to get more Think Story videos.

00:11:06.260 --> 00:11:09.000
You can also find me
on Twitter @ThinkStoryYT.

00:11:09.180 --> 00:11:10.600
And until next time remember,

00:11:10.780 --> 00:11:12.080
Daddy loves you very much.

